      <div id="sutta">
              <h2 id="SN11.15" class="h1">A Delightful Place<br/>
                Rāmaṇeyyaka Sutta  (SN 11:15)</h2>
<p>On one occasion the Blessed One was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. Then Sakka the deva-king went to the Blessed One and, on arrival, having bowed down to him, stood to one side. As he was standing there, he said to the Blessed One, “What, lord, is a delightful place?”</p>
<div class="verse">
<p class="vspk">The Buddha:</p>
<p>“Park shrines, forest shrines,</p>
<p>well-constructed lotus ponds</p>
<p>aren’t worth one-sixteenth</p>
<p>of a delightful human being.</p>
<div class="verse-add">
<p>In village or wilds,</p>
<p>valley, plateau:</p>
<p>that place is delightful</p>
<p>where arahants dwell.”<span class="fn"><a href="#sn11.15note01">1</a></span><!--end fn cite--></p>
</div><!--end verse-add-->
</div><!--end verse-->
              <div class="note">
                <p class="notetitle">Note</p><!--end notetitle-->
<p id="sn11.15note01">1. This second verse = <a href="../KN/Dhp/Ch07.html#dhp098" class="sutta-ref">Dhp 98</a>.</p>
              </div><!--end notes-->

      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
